<question type="description"><name><text>Module 3 · Lesson 11 · Section 7: The Story — Part 11</text></name><questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[<h3>Section 7: The Story — Part 11</h3>
<p><strong>The Healing</strong></p>
<p><em>Narrative note: The king, having fallen ill, begs for physical
and spiritual salvation. Notice the dense use of verbal suffixes (fast
direct objects) as he pleads with Yukhannan.</em></p>
<p><strong>Sentence 1</strong></p>
<p>ܘܒܝܘܡܐ ܗ̣ܘ ܢܦܠ ܡܠܟܐ ܒܟܘܪܗܢܐ ܒܝܫܐ w-b-yūmā haw npal malkā b-kurhānā
bīšā. w-b-yūmā (and-in-day) haw (that) npal (fell) malkā (the-king)
b-kurhānā (in-illness) bīšā (evil/bad). → And in that day, the king fell
into a severe illness.</p>
<p><strong>Sentence 2</strong></p>
<p>ܘܐܬܐ ܠܘܬ ܝܘܚܢܢ ܘܢܦܠ ܩܕܡܘܗܝ ܘܐܡܪ ܠܗ w-ʾetā l-wāt Yūḥannan, w-npal
qdāmāw-hy, w-ʾemar l-ēh: w-ʾetā (and-came) l-wāt (to-the-presence-of)
Yūḥannan (John), w-npal (and-fell) qdāmāw-hy (before-him), w-ʾemar
(and-said) l-ēh (to-him): → And he came to Yukhannan, and fell before
him, and said to him:</p>
<p><strong>Sentence 3</strong></p>
<p>ܐܣܝܢܝ ܡܢ ܟܘܪܗܢܝ ܘܦܪܩܢܝ ܡܢ ܡܘܬܐ ʾasy-anī men kurhān-y, w-parq-anī men
mawtā! ʾasy-anī (heal-me [Aphel Impv]) men (from) kurhān-y (illness-my),
w-parq-anī (and-save-me [Peal Impv]) men (from) mawtā (death)! → “Heal
me from my illness, and save me from death!”</p>
<p><strong>Sentence 4</strong></p>
<p>ܘܫܒܘܩ ܠܝ ܚܛܝܬܝ ܕܣܓܝܐܐ ܗܝ w-šbūq lī ḥṭītt-y d-saggīʾā hī! w-šbūq
(and-forgive [Peal Impv]) lī (to-me) ḥṭītt-y (sin-my) d-saggīʾā
(which-is-great/much) hī (she-[is])! → “And forgive me my sin, which is
great!”</p>
<p><strong>Sentence 5</strong></p>
<p>ܩܪܳܘܗܝ ܝܘܚܢܢ ܠܐܠܗܐ ܘܐܡܪ qrāwhy Yūḥannan l-Alāhā w-ʾemar: qrāwhy
(he-called-him [3msg Peal Perf. of q-r-y + 3msg obj. suffix]) Yūḥannan
(John) l-Alāhā (to-God) w-ʾemar (and-said): → Yukhannan called upon God
and said: <em>Note: III-Yodh verbs contract the final yodh before the
suffix: qrā + -wh + y → qrāwhy.</em></p>
<p><strong>Sentence 6</strong></p>
<p>ܐܠܗܐ ܢܚܬܟ ܘܢܚܝܝܟ ܗܫܐ Alāhā nneḥt-āḵ, w-naḥyē-ḵ hāšā. Alāhā (God)
nneḥt-āḵ (he-will-give-rest-you), w-naḥyē-ḵ
(and-he-will-give-life/save-you [Aphel Imperfect]) hāšā (now). → “God
will give you rest, and will save you now.”</p>
<p><strong>Sentence 7</strong></p>
<p>ܘܐܣܝܗ ܐܠܗܐ ܒܛܝܒܘܬܗ w-ʾasy-eh Alāhā b-ṭaybūtt-eh. w-ʾasy-eh
(and-he-healed-him) Alāhā (God) b-ṭaybūtt-eh (by-grace-his). → And God
healed him by his grace.</p>
<hr />

]]></text></questiontext></question>
